# The monitor starts after 13 days without running (BACKFILL_MAX_AGE_S, the longest gap it fills). The detector's log holds
# one sample a minute for all of it. The monitor reads all 31 log pages as base64 text, cuts about 1870 bins, keeps the newest
# 1008 (YAR-025), saves the state file after every bin, and then sends the backlog 144 slots every 10 minutes: 2 simulated hours
# cover the fill and the first sends. link_bps is an assumption (USB serial bulk transfers of the firmware's 192-byte chunks).
source yarrow
interval 600
hours 2
cpm 20
seed 1
absent_hours 312
link_bps 100000
